WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.590
August 2015.

2
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.090
Fires begin to burn in Indonesia.

3
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.330
That year, more than 2.6
million hectares of forest,

4
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.710
peat and other land burned.

5
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.070
In September and October, fires
across maritime Southeast Asia,

6
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:22.530
mostly in Indonesia, averaged
11.3 million tonnes of CO₂ a day.

7
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.110
Fossil fuels in the 28 EU
countries: 8.9 million.

8
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.730
Who pays when one country's
smoke crosses borders?

9
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.770
The companies that lit the fires?

10
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.630
No one, because smoke disperses?

11
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.710
In this mission, you'll unpick the causes:

12
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.690
a human trigger, drained
peat, and an El Niño drought.

13
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:47.950
Then you'll judge the responses, from a
regional agreement to peatland protection.

14
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.850
Your mission: find out who pays when
one country's smoke crosses borders.
